  "articleSummary": "The article argues that AI agents are useless without integrations into business systems like Salesforce or Jira, and proposes the Model Context Protocol (MCP) as a standardization solution akin to USB-C for cables. It explains that MCP eliminates the need for custom API wrappers by implementing a single communication protocol, enabling agents to connect to any MCP-compatible service. The piece provides a technical tutorial using Mastra's `MCPClient` to set up multiple integrations, connect tools to agents, and handle per-user authentication, warning against hardcoding credentials. Written in an analytical, solution-oriented tone for developers, it frames MCP as a practical standard that simplifies the traditionally messy integration process.",
